invariant: INV-16
file: sha512.h
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh arm64-hash-count
reason: sha512.h's sha512_on_instructions reads CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA256,
  the bit of another hash's instructions. An arm64 caller that states the
  SHA-256 instructions alone then runs SHA-384 on instructions it never
  stated, and its CPU may have FEAT_SHA256 without FEAT_SHA512, where the
  session dies of SIGILL. The bytes are the same either way.
  bin/hash_runtime_test runs every row under each of the 128 values the
  seven bits beside CH_CPU_PROBED make, which hold each bit with and
  without the other, and counts each hash's calls apart. Only an arm64
  object compiles this predicate, so the catch is the script, which runs
  the arm64 binaries under qemu-aarch64. The lane skips without docker,
  and this then reports unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
    return (cpu & CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA512) != 0;
--- new
    return (cpu & CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA256) != 0;
